DIAGNOSTIC ONLY -- not a fix, not meant to ship. Instruments the two
`amd::Os::yield()` spin sites in rocvirtual.hpp closest matching the
strace evidence for the HIP-graph-replay deadlock on gfx803 (see
SESSION_HANDOFF.md section on the graph-replay investigation): a live
repro's stuck thread spins on `sched_yield()` every ~35-40us, zero other
syscalls, forever. `VirtualGPU::WaitForQueueSlot()` (hardware-queue
read-index spin, no per-iteration blocking call) matches that cadence;
`WaitForSignal()`'s active-wait loop (each iteration blocks up to 4s
inside `signal_wait_scacquire` before it can even reach the yield) does
not, but is instrumented too for confirmation since it costs nothing.

Prints every 5,000,000 spins (WaitForQueueSlot) / every 5 loops
(WaitForSignal, ~20s at its ~4s-per-iteration cadence) to stderr with
the diagnostic state (queue read/write index, capacity, signal handle),
so a stuck repro's container logs identify which site is actually
spinning without needing amd-dbgapi/rocgdb (unavailable in this
container, see SESSION_HANDOFF.md section 9/11).

